    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (82.01) and **Mickey Moniak** (73.71), our premier plays for this slate. **Corbin Carroll** capitalizes on a high-upside matchup against Sandy Alcantara; while Alcantara remains a test for any hitter, the dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable park shift vault **Corbin Carroll** into our highest-scoring slot. **Mickey Moniak** is the statistical standout of the day, with a massive +14% boost from park factors and platoon splits against Mize, making him a primary target for counting stats. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Seiya Suzuki** also provide solid contributions, with **Gabriel Moreno** benefiting from a high spot in the order, while **Seiya Suzuki**\u2019s +8% order bump keeps his efficiency firmly in the \"Strong\" start territory.\n\nWe are navigating a few \"Marginal\" starts at the bottom of the card, specifically with **Josh Naylor**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Zach McKinstry**, who are all hovering near the 40-point floor. **Josh Naylor** faces a difficult matchup against Detmers, suffering a -16% SP skill hit, while **Jose Caballero** and **Zach McKinstry** are hampered by late-order placement and diminished platoon efficiency. The most difficult decision rested with **Cole Young**, who fell just short at 38.82 points. His case for a start was bolstered by a \"Slow SP\" advantage that could have facilitated an opportunistic stolen base, but the overall SP skill penalty associated with Detmers ultimately kept him on the bench. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Griffin Conine**, whose 61.48 score is propped up significantly by a favorable matchup against Burnes\u2019 7.87 xERA; if Burnes finds his command, that floor could drop quickly. We continue to monitor the status of **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Tyler Soderstrom**, both of whom remain unavailable as we look to maximize our remaining games.",
